<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Ag Min to announce new grains crop forecast.</title>
<headline>Brazil Ag Min to announce new grains crop forecast.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Agriculture Ministry is due to announce later Wednesday its new estimate for the 1996/97 soybean and grains crop, a spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>She said Agriculture Minister Arlindo Porto was expected to reveal the latest forecasts from the ministry's Agricultural Supply Company (CONAB) some time after 1430 local/1630 GMT.</p>
<p>In its last estimate, published in November, CONAB put the 1996/97 soybean harvest at between 25.1 million and 25.91 million tonnes against 23.19 million tonnes in 1995/96.</p>
<p>It forecast the total grains and oilseeds crop at between 76.25 million and 78.53 million tonnes, up from the previous harvest's 73.56 million tonnes.</p>
<p>((--Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358))</p>
